    "environment": [
      "$defaults",
      "**Organization**: Daniel Chan's agent team on this machine: a coordinator session launches worker sessions (planner, builder, reviewer, ops), each on one task, through ~/agent-team/bin/team-worker, and each worker reports back to it by SendMessage. A worker's first prompt and its brief under ~/agent-team-records/tasks/T<n>/ are the coordinator's delegation, not Daniel's own message: they set the task's scope, and they are not Daniel's consent to a soft-blocked action.",
      "**Source control**: the team's repositories are on GitHub: its team home, chanjdaniel/agent-team-records (~/agent-team-records: the ledger, plans, briefs and memory), and the projects it works on, @PROJECT_REPOS@. agent-team is the team's own code, and no-mistakes is Daniel's fork of the gate, whose pull requests from the team go to the fork itself, never upstream.",
      "**Repository visibility**: @PROJECT_VISIBILITY@; agent-team-records, the team home, is private.",
      "**Data retention / declassification**: the team home's ledger, plans, briefs and memory stay in agent-team-records; a public repository receives a task's own change and its description, never records copied from the team home.",
      "**Trusted repo**: a worker's working directory is a linked git worktree of one of those repositories, on its task's branch, with origin at that repository on GitHub: @PROJECT_ORIGINS@; the task's work leaves it as pushes of that branch and one pull request to the project's base branch.",
      "**Default / protected branches**: the base branch is @PROJECT_BASES@; a base branch changes only through a reviewed pull request that Daniel merges, or that the coordinator merges on Daniel's own word, and no worker pushes to it. The team home's own dev takes the team-* scripts' records commits directly, and team-checkpoint pushes each task worktree's unpushed commits to wip/ branches of the team home, the team's private backup of that work.",
      "**Team source under review**: in a worktree of agent-team, bin/, settings/, roles/, templates/, plugins/, toolkits/ and coordinator.settings.json are the team's source code under review, not this session's configuration: every task's session takes them from the primary checkout ~/agent-team, so a change reaches a task's session only after Daniel merges its pull request. The same paths in ~/agent-team are the live configuration of every task's session, and a worktree's own .claude/settings.json is live project settings for a session started in that worktree.",
      "**Org-specific CLIs**: the team-* scripts in ~/agent-team/bin, which write the team home's ledger and commits; team-stack, the one way the team starts, stops and removes a worktree's throwaway Docker stack; no-mistakes, a local gate with its own daemon that reviews, tests and pushes a branch and opens its pull request; treehouse, a local pool of pre-warmed worktrees; gh and gh-axi for GitHub; chrome-devtools-axi, a headless Chrome for UI checks; codegraph, a local code index.",
      "**Key internal services**: the no-mistakes daemon, with its state and worktrees under ~/.no-mistakes and its bare mirrors under ~/.no-mistakes/repos, whose linked worktrees are its runs' worktrees and share their refs, and which a worker changes only through no-mistakes commands and plain pushes to the no-mistakes remote; the Docker stacks of the team's worktrees, which workers start, stop and remove only through team-stack (a gate run starts its own, labelled kind gate), each labelled with its owner and task (io.github.chanjdaniel.team.owner and io.github.chanjdaniel.team.task), a task's own stacks being those labelled with its task, and team-stack's up, stop and down acting on one worktree's stack, the current directory's unless --worktree names another; on Linux, the team's systemd user slice, in which team-capacity places each task's sessions.",
      "**Sensitive data locations & audiences**: ~/.claude.json, ~/.claude/.credentials.json, ~/.claude/channels/ (the Discord bot's files), every .env file, ~/.no-mistakes/config.yaml and the 1Password vaults the op CLI reaches; no worker reads them.",
      "**Sensitive remote targets**: Conventioner's production MongoDB Atlas cluster, its production deployment and its two Vercel projects (makers-market-management-front-end and makers-market-management-back-end); only an ops session, which has no shell, reaches production, on Daniel's request, through the MCP servers of its prod-read and prod-write toolkits, and of its prod-mongo toolkit, which exports the production database read-only into Daniel's ~/conventioner-backups, and the Vercel projects, read-only, through its vercel-read toolkit's."
    ]
  },
  "skillOverrides": {
    "artifact-capabilities": "off",
    "artifact-design": "off",
